- `TestEnsureMetadataBranch_NoopWhenCustomRefAlreadyExists` — pre-populate both refs; assert migration short-circuits and neither ref is rewritten.
- `TestEnsureMetadataBranch_DivergedRefs_CustomRefWins` — both refs at different hashes; assert migration skips and the custom ref is authoritative.
- `TestEnsureMetadataBranch_FreshRepoV1_1_CreatesOrphan` — no legacy branch, no custom ref; assert custom ref created as fresh orphan.
- `TestEnsureMetadataBranch_LegacyOnly_V1Mode_LegacyBranchUsed` — confirm migration doesn't trigger when settings say v1.
- `TestEnsureMetadataBranch_ReadOfLegacyFails_FallsBackToFreshOrphan` — corrupt the legacy ref; assert WARN log, custom ref created fresh, legacy branch untouched.

### Push refactor (`push_common_test.go`)

- `TestPushRefIfNeeded_BranchPathStillWorks` — preserve coverage of the existing branch-based push.
- `TestPushRefIfNeeded_CustomRefPath` — same scenarios at the 1.1 ref pair: no-op when local matches tracking, push when ahead, rebase recovery on non-FF.
- `TestFetchAndRebaseSessions_CustomRef` — cherry-pick-onto-remote works correctly at the custom ref pair.

### Setup flow (new `setup_v1_metadata_ref_test.go`)

- `TestRunSetupFlow_FreshRepo_WritesV1MetadataRef` — fresh temp repo, in-process setup writes `checkpoints_version: 1.1`.
- `TestRunSetupFlow_FreshRepo_InstallsFetchRefspec` — refspec appended to `remote.origin.fetch`; running twice does not duplicate it.
